
1) Add new themes: "Army" with green/brown colors and "ArmyChalk" font and "Hacker" with "BigBlue_TerminalPlus Nerd Font Mono". It should be possible to assign fonts which are not in the recommended list.

2) The font_weight under button groups should be exposed in the config.toml as well. I expect to see the font_weight bold under [themes.RedmondDark.number] and [themes.RedmondLight.number]

3) Make all the button groups in CupertinoDark and CupertinoLight to have font_weight "regular" setting while the theme itself preserves the "light" setting for places which are not the button groups

4) There should be a 4th column for the colors for the button groups, which is the 2nd toggled state fill, font, border colors. Every button group should have this, even if there is no secondary function assigned for them, since the layout can be changed. The "second" button group which hosts the "2nd" button should get it's toggled color from this column instead how it is done right now (it is not exposed in the config, but somehow derived (maybe inverted) from the existing colors).

5) Rename "debug_raw_formula" to "ascii_mode" in the config.toml

6) When the user pastes something from the clipboard check the contents before deciding how to paste it. If it has operators and other stuff then overwrite what is on the current display (current behavior). If it's a number (with or without a decimal dot or comma) then just paste it as an operand, so in this case if the user already types "52" then the pasted number should replace that, but if the user typed "52+" then it should come after the plus sign. So the last operand (empty or not) should be from the clipboard if its a number. If it's a too big number, then silently ignore the paste (I think this is the current behavior but test it).

7) The font size scaling is not accurate. This might be because it depends on the font itself, but we should always use the available horizontal and vertival space efficiently regardless of which font is used. Right now if I paste in a really long number e.g.: "99999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999999" it will be smaller than it should be and only using about 80% of the horizontal space. Also, some fonts which have italic effect by default on the regular weight (e.g. Monte Carlo) will go out from the main display area on the right (the first character). It looks like the bottom of the font is correctly aligned but the top is not checked.

8) Add a slider in the settings side panel which configures when we change to scientific notation. The range should be 2 - 99 (default 15). Of course this needs to saved in config.toml as well.

